From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: hda/conexant: Add quirk for Huawei MateBook YTG-XXX

The headphone jack is not detected on this Huawei MateBook (Conexant
SN6140 codec, subsystem 0x19e5:0x3e6d). The BIOS marks pin 0x18 as
[N/A], so the HDA parser reports hp_outs=0 and userspace never gets a
"Headphones" output. The jack itself is wired and functional:
GET_PIN_SENSE on NID 0x18 returns 0x80000000 (presence) when a plug is
inserted, and pin 0x18 advertises "IN OUT HP EAPD Detect".

Reuse the existing Huawei MateBook pin-config fixup, which configures
NID 0x18 as a headphone jack (0x03211020) and restores detection and
speaker auto-mute.

This applies on top of commit d152afd1cd7a6 ("ALSA: hda/conexant: Add
pin config quirk for Huawei Matebook"), which added the fixup and the
quirk for subsystem 0x19e5:0x3289.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.com>
---
 sound/hda/codecs/conexant.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/hda/codecs/conexant.c b/sound/hda/codecs/conexant.c
--- a/sound/hda/codecs/conexant.c
+++ b/sound/hda/codecs/conexant.c
@@ -1143,6 +1143,7 @@ static const struct hda_quirk cxt5066_fixups[] = {
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x17aa, 0x3978, "Lenovo G50-70", CXT_FIXUP_STEREO_DMIC),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x17aa, 0x397b, "Lenovo S205", CXT_FIXUP_STEREO_DMIC),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK_VENDOR(0x17aa, "Thinkpad/Ideapad", CXT_FIXUP_LENOVO_XPAD_ACPI),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x19e5, 0x3289, "Huawei Matebook", CXT_FIXUP_HUAWEI_MATEBOOK_HP),
+	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x19e5, 0x3e6d, "Huawei MateBook YTG-XXX", CXT_FIXUP_HUAWEI_MATEBOOK_HP),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1c06, 0x2011, "Lemote A1004", CXT_PINCFG_LEMOTE_A1004),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1c06, 0x2012, "Lemote A1205", CXT_PINCFG_LEMOTE_A1205),
 	SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1d05, 0x3012, "MECHREVO Wujie 15X Pro", CXT_FIXUP_HEADSET_MIC),
-- 
